ves/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"646c3df85b480fd57618a32bba46ecd394b2d7f9fdf1584ade0f7b08db41c52f","quote":"Following completion of the Proposed Transaction, Santersus will become a wholly owned subsidiary of Xenetic. The combined company is expected to be led by James Ladtkow, Chief Executive Officer of Santersus, together with the current Santersus management team. Xenetic Biosciences, Inc. is expected to be renamed Santersus Bio, Inc., with corporate headquarters in Framingham, Massachusetts. The combined company’s Board of Directors is expected to be composed of eight members, including two nominees from Xenetic and six nominees from Santersus.","context":"The key equity holders, directors and officers of Xenetic, as well as certain parties identified by Santersus, have signed lock-up agreements restricting transfers of the combined company’s stock for 180 days post-closing, subject to limited exceptions.","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":39,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"2dee249ac7d330a472025883697605e67102617ec0ebaf152f7e37b0a06eac12","quote":"The Proposed Transaction has been unanimously approved by the Board of Directors of Santersus. Xenetic’s Board of Directors – acting on the unanimous recommendation of its independent Special Committee – has also approved the Proposed Transaction and recommends that Xenetic stockholders vote in favor of the Proposed Transaction. The Proposed Transaction is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2026, subject to approval by Xenetic stockholders, the shares of Xenetic common stock issuable in the Proposed Transaction having been approved for listing on Nasdaq, the effectiveness of a resale registration statement on Form S-1 to be filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (“SEC”), and the satisfaction or waiver of other customary closing conditions.","context":"Following completion of the Proposed Transaction, Santersus will become a wholly owned subsidiary of Xenetic. The combined company is expected to be led by James Ladtkow, Chief Executive Officer of Santersus, together with the current Santersus management team. Xenetic Biosciences, Inc. is expected to be renamed Santersus Bio, Inc., with corporate headquarters in Framingham, Massachusetts. The combined company’s Board of Directors is expected to be composed of eight members, including two nominees from Xenetic and six nominees from Santersus.","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":40,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"15ed928583efcbda7745f0820434f2b398774e2335372dd551b4cdc143b1383a","quote":"Mintz, Levin, Cohn, Ferris, Glovsky and Popeo, P.C. is serving as U.S. legal advisor to Santersus and Lex Futura AG is serving as Swiss legal counsel to Santersus. Holland & Knight LLP is serving as legal advisor to Xenetic, and Canaccord Genuity is serving as financial advisor to Xenetic.","context":"The Proposed Transaction has been unanimously approved by the Board of Directors of Santersus. Xenetic’s Board of Directors – acting on the unanimous recommendation of its independent Special Committee – has also approved the Proposed Transaction and recommends that Xenetic stockholders vote in favor of the Proposed Transaction. The Proposed Transaction is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2026, subject to approval by Xenetic stockholders, the shares of Xenetic common stock issuable in the Proposed Transaction having been approved for listing on Nasdaq, the effectiveness of a resale registration statement on Form S-1 to be filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (“SEC”), and the satisfaction or waiver of other customary closing conditions.","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":41,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"656ad2c4fe9532d34fe4094eacdf47aa627be3795d7b337187a3a3ff01359607","quote":"Additional information about the transaction will be provided in a Current Report on Form 8-K that will be filed by Xenetic with the SEC and will be available at http://www.sec.gov.","context":"Mintz, Levin, Cohn, Ferris, Glovsky and Popeo, P.C. is serving as U.S. legal advisor to Santersus and Lex Futura AG is serving as Swiss legal counsel to Santersus. Holland & Knight LLP is serving as legal advisor to Xenetic, and Canaccord Genuity is serving as financial advisor to Xenetic.","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":42,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"654ce7668112ff5676229f6dd41ce9f476f93f188f85016466d4c887da5d29b6","quote":"Xenetic Biosciences, Inc. is a biopharmaceutical company focused on advancing innovative immuno-oncology technologies addressing difficult to treat cancers. The Company's proprietary DNase technology is designed to improve outcomes of existing treatments, including immunotherapies, by targeting neutrophil extracellular traps (NETs), which are involved in cancer progression. Xenetic is currently focused on advancing its systemic DNase program into the clinic as an adjunctive therapy for pancreatic carcinoma and locally advanced or metastatic solid tumors.","context":"About Xenetic Biosciences","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":45,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"9ca323b0ef93103e1d80e94924c6f98dc7e977c9f16c13370b01379587a21d43","quote":"For more information, please visit the Company's website at www.xeneticbio.com and connect on X, LinkedIn, and Facebook.","context":"Xenetic Biosciences, Inc. is a biopharmaceutical company focused on advancing innovative immuno-oncology technologies addressing difficult to treat cancers. The Company's proprietary DNase technology is designed to improve outcomes of existing treatments, including immunotherapies, by targeting neutrophil extracellular traps (NETs), which are involved in cancer progression. Xenetic is currently focused on advancing its systemic DNase program into the clinic as an adjunctive therapy for pancreatic carcinoma and locally advanced or metastatic solid tumors.","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":46,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c.bin","sha256":"9bc659431516287283623025b36039488c2ac2b9d096d078bfe021ed77310b0c"}},{"id":"4bddf18656e9f275b77cc3dda489dde6b4fb84657c239559ddc1c82cbeceab26","quote":"Santersus AG is a therapeutic medical device company developing NucleoCapture® - its selective extracorporeal blood purification platform designed to selectively remove neutrophil extracellular traps (NETs) to treat acute and chronic conditions across critical care, autoimmunity and transplantation. For more information, please visit www.santersus.com.","context":"About Santersus AG","section":"Business Update Conference Call and Webcast","block":48,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001683168-26-007181","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-09-14","cik":"0001534525","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1534525/000168316826007181/xenetic_ex9901.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9bc6594315162